menu "PIV smart-card token"

config WOZ_PIV_CCID
	bool "Expose a native-USB PIV/CCID token (VM bench only)"
	depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
	default n
	help
	  Enumerate the ESP32-S3 native USB-OTG port as a single-slot CCID
	  smart-card reader containing a PIV application.

	  Keep this OFF for ordinary firmware development. A host Mac can claim a
	  PIV device during enumeration and offer to pair it with a local account.
	  Enable it only for tightly controlled validation in the disposable
	  Parallels macOS guest, with the board's separate USB-UART connection kept
	  available for flashing and recovery.

	  This initial option does not alter LoginWindow or enforce smart-card
	  authentication. Account pairing remains a separate, explicit VM step.

endmenu
